    "body": "## Scope\n\nAdd the narrow server-side readback needed after an ambiguous participant-token replacement response.\n\n- `GET /v1/admin/battles/{battleId}/capabilities/{side}/status` returns only `generation` and `status` for one side.\n- A dedicated `OPERATOR_READ_TOKEN` with a minimum 32-character secret authorizes the route independently of `ADMIN_CONTROL_TOKEN`; missing or incorrect read keys fail closed.\n- Reject every `Origin`, `OPTIONS`/preflight, and non-GET method; responses use `Cache-Control: no-store` and do not emit CORS headers.\n- The route reads only the requested capability row. It never returns bearer/digest/participant/recovery data and never changes state.\n- No schema or migration changes. Existing participant GET/commit and admin revoke/replace remain unchanged.\n\n## Local verification\n\n- `node --check` for Worker and local API test: PASS.\n- `python3 -m unittest gameplay-server/test/test_chat03b2_capability_operator_lifecycle_sql.py`: 2/2 PASS.\n- Full disposable local Worker/workerd/D1 profile `node gameplay-server/test/private_api_local_test.mjs`: `CHAT03B2_LOCAL_PRIVATE_API_PASS (NOT PRODUCTION_AUTH_PASS)`.\n- Added coverage for separate read authorization, absent/wrong keys, malformed/missing battle and side, active/revoked sides, no Origin/CORS/preflight, GET-only behavior, no-store, exact response/secret minimization, no D1 writes, and parallel read/replace.\n- Lost-response scenario: the test drops a successful replace response, reads generation/status over HTTP, verifies the read did not alter D1 or disclose the lost token, then explicitly calls the existing replace route at the observed generation. The readback does not recover plaintext or trigger a replacement.\n- `git diff --check`: PASS.\n\n## Baseline and boundary\n\nBase: `main@31b7a077820914e92de81239e5ab4099e3dfa558`.\n\nNo Cloudflare resources, keys, staging, deployment, main changes, Stage 7.15, or edits to PR #449, #450, or #451. This does not close other private-alpha gates or claim hosted, production, Safari, or two-device acceptance. Keep Draft for exact-head CI and independent review.",
